offscreen, deferred and shadowmappingomni list the frame's draw command
buffer in their submission and then push it again: one primary command
buffer twice in a batch, without SIMULTANEOUS_USE (VUID-vkQueueSubmit-
pCommandBuffers-00071). RADV chains a batch's command buffers and loops
forever inside vkQueueSubmit on it, on the host and so in the device's
executor. Submitted once, as the other samples do.

diff --git a/deferred/deferred.cpp b/deferred/deferred.cpp
index 90585d6..51e32ec 100644
--- a/deferred/deferred.cpp
+++ b/deferred/deferred.cpp
@@ -1200,7 +1200,6 @@ public:
 			offScreenCmdBuffer,
 			drawCmdBuffers[currentBuffer],
 		};
-		submitCmdBuffers.push_back(drawCmdBuffers[currentBuffer]);
 		submitInfo.commandBufferCount = submitCmdBuffers.size();
 		submitInfo.pCommandBuffers = submitCmdBuffers.data();
 
